/output/facets-trellis/
# GIT-03: same PHI reasoning as /output/facets-trellis/ above -- these are the private
# upstream inputs to code/archive/sanitize_facets.R (itself gitignored), which produces
# the PHI-free output/facets-trellis-public/ and output/facets-public/ that
# scripts/build_public.sh actually copies into the release. Not read by _targets.R or
# any verify_*.R script (tests/verify_artifacts.R explicitly excludes this path).
/output/facets/merge-facets-tables.R/
# GIT-03: PHI -- raw PGDX vendor mutation reports. code/pgdx_reports.rmd (its generator)
# is marked PRIVATE/never-publish in code/CLAUDE.md and excluded by build_public.sh;
# this output was never covered by the same exclusion. No downstream reader.
/output/pgdx_reports.rmd/
# Private BAM inventory
/missing_bams.txt
# Generated site assets (rebuilt by wflow_build(); Bucket A)
# GIT-03: same Bucket A reasoning -- table Rmd outputs and top-level HTML pages
# rebuilt by wflow_build(). table_s1/s3/s9 have no format="file" target in _targets.R,
# so nothing needs them pre-tracked; they build fine from a fresh clone or CI.
# MAN-04: table_s6/s7/s8's .tsv/.csv siblings are NOT ignored (see "NOT ignored"
# block below) -- they are format="file" _targets.R inputs (amp_file, wes_cnv_file,
# del_file) that tar_make() reads *before* wflow_build() ever runs in CI, so keeping
# only the source .Rmd/.html ignored here is correct but the data files must stay
# tracked, same as table_s4/table_s5.
/docs/table/table_s1.Rmd/
/docs/table/table_s3.Rmd/
/docs/table/table_s9.Rmd/
# NOT ignored, deliberately: docs/table/table_s2.Rmd|table_s4.Rmd|table_s5.Rmd/ and
# docs/{table_s2,table_s4,table_s5,ext-figure2}.html. CI's "Build workflowr analysis
# pages" step explicitly skips rebuilding table_s2/s4/s5.Rmd (private coverage/mutation
# inputs) and ext-figure2.Rmd (live UniProt API call) -- a fresh/CI clone has no way to
# reproduce these, and _targets.R reads table_s2/s4/s5's outputs back as format="file"
# targets (s2file/s3file/s4file), so they must stay committed. docs/about.html and
# docs/table_s0.html also stay tracked -- no current source Rmd renders either one
# (about.html: analysis/_site.yml links it but no analysis/about.Rmd exists;
# table_s0.html: no matching Rmd found at all) -- an editorial gap, not a GIT-03 call.
# docs/.nojekyll also stays tracked -- a one-time GitHub Pages marker, not something
# wflow_build() recreates on a normal run.
# Manuscript LaTeX build artifacts (rebuilt by make pdf; Bucket A)
# NOTE: hallberg2025.pdf is kept tracked intentionally.
